  "title": {
    "text": "Rural regions are older, and older, rural regions churn less",
    "subtitle": [
      "ITL2 regions: population density against median age (correlation -0.88), coloured by job reallocation rate; all pooled over 2018\u201324.",
      "Darker = more churn; grey line = fit across all regions. The dense, young regions (London, big cities) churn most; sparse, older regions least.",
      "Sources: ONS Longitudinal Business Database (Secure Access, SN 9501); ONS, NRS and NISRA population estimates; authors' calculations."
    ]
  },
